  "id": "Compound::DB02300 - Gene::7421",
  "verbalization": "Calcipotriol, through its structural similarities to other steroid compounds, is linked to Vdr via a series of biochemical pathways that ultimately involve the binding of calcidiol or related compounds. The evidence suggests that Calcipotriol, as a member of the vitamin D family, interacts with Vdr through a common ancestor in the steroid biosynthetic pathway. This connection is reinforced by the fact that Calcipotriol and its analogs, such as Alfacalcidol and Dihydrotachysterol, share a common structural motif that leads to their binding with Vdr. The lowest common ancestors in these relationships highlight a shared pathway involving secondary alcohols and polyols, which are critical in the metabolism and action of steroid hormones. The integration of these pathways implies that Calcipotriol exerts its effects on Vdr through a mechanism that involves the conversion of precursor molecules into active forms, ultimately influencing the regulation of calcium homeostasis and bone health.",
